    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast, multicentric (2.6 cm at 10 o&apos;clock and 0.8 cm at 7 o&apos;clock), grade 2, estrogen and progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative, pT2(m) pN0(sn) M0, anatomic stage IIA, recurrence score 13; suspected at presentation, confirmed by core biopsy four days later, and treated by right total mastectomy with sentinel node biopsy; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the documented 1811 breast disease and mastectomy, whose cancer diagnosis is debated</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>C50.411</td><td>S — Synthetic diagnosis confirmed by biopsy and surgical pathology in the modern episode; whether her historical disease was cancer remains a retrospective interpretation (R).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Estrogen receptor positive status of the breast cancer (ER 95 percent, PR 70 percent)</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z17.0</td><td>S — Synthetic receptor result; no tissue from her lifetime was examined.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Absence of the right breast after total mastectomy without reconstruction, her choice</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z90.11</td><td>S — Synthetic coding of the modern mastectomy, which echoes the documented operation.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Long-term use of anastrozole as adjuvant endocrine therapy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z79.811</td><td>S — Synthetic treatment status.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Low bone mass (osteopenia) on baseline DXA before anastrozole: lumbar spine T-score -1.4, femoral neck -1.7; 10-year major osteoporotic fracture risk about 8 percent (FRAX); vitamin D insufficiency</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>M85.80</td><td>S — Synthetic finding on the baseline DXA the protocol requires for an aromatase inhibitor.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-6">
    <td>Seroma under the right mastectomy flap after drain removal, without infection; aspirated once by the breast surgery team; resolved</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>L76.34</td><td>S — Synthetic common complication of the synthetic mastectomy; it does not echo a documented illness.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

