    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. Depression screen negative; AUDIT-C 2, below the threshold for women. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Right breast cancer after mastectomy, on anastrozole (C50.411)</content>. Recovering well; no side effects of anastrozole yet. [S]<list><item>Continue anastrozole and vitamin D.</item><item>Survivorship visit in three months.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Cardiovascular risk</content>. LDL cholesterol 132 mg/dL, total 214, HDL 58 ten days ago; blood pressure 120/76; non-smoker; no diabetes. Estimated 10-year cardiovascular risk below 5 percent. [S]<list><item>No statin; diet and activity.</item><item>Lipids rechecked yearly on anastrozole.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 1811-1812</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; recommended from age 50; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Dose 1 today; dose 2 in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 1811-1812</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; she will get it at her pharmacy in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended for adults 19 to 59; series to start at the next visit if the screening test shows no immunity</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six and a half years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Replaced by surveillance: yearly diagnostic mammogram of the left breast from next August</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Cytology with HPV co-testing three years ago, normal; next in two years</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Colonoscopy eight years ago, normal; next at ten years</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>DXA ten days ago: low bone mass; repeat in two years on anastrozole</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening; no prior result on record; drawn today, results pending</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Lipid panel ten days ago reviewed; 10-year risk below 5 percent; no statin</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 23.9 without other risk factors</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>120/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 2, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity and diet counseling</td><td>Completed today</td><td>150 minutes of walking a week, strength exercise twice a week once the surgeon allows, and calcium from food</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1811-1812 season; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV results by portal message. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Survivorship visit in three months. [S]</paragraph></text>

